course: dictionary
lesson: 465
title: Army: soldiers or a huge crowd
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An army is a large group of soldiers trained to fight on land for a country. Read the words around it to be sure which meaning you need. «George Washington led the American army to victory» is about soldiers, because leading to victory means winning a war.
explain: The word can also mean a very large group of people or animals doing something together. Look at «an army of ants» or «an army of volunteers». The clue is the word of, and the sense of a huge number. Ask yourself: is this about soldiers, or is it about a crowd?
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Many countries sent weapons, training and money to Ukraine's army but did not send their own soldiers to fight.» Army fits here as soldiers fighting for a country. A band of musicians would not make sense, so you know which meaning is right.
fact: An army is a large group of soldiers trained to fight on land for a country.
fact: «Armies» is the plural, so one army, many armies.
fact: «An army of ants» means a very large group of ants working together.
fact: The Terracotta Army near Xi'an was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well.
fact: Its thousands of life-size clay soldiers have different faces and hairstyles.
exercise: «The Terracotta Army near Xi'an was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well.» Who found the Terracotta Army? | Children playing in a park | Archaeologists in a museum | Soldiers on a march | *Farmers digging a well
exercise: «George Washington led the American army to victory and became the first president in 1789.» What is an army in this sentence? | A group of musicians playing together | A shop that sells weapons | *A large group of soldiers trained to fight for a country | A huge crowd of tourists
exercise: Which phrase means a huge number of ants working together? | A nest of ants | A line of ants | One ant alone | *An army of ants
test: «Many countries sent weapons, training and money to Ukraine's army but did not send their own soldiers to fight.» What does army mean here? | A band of singers | A team of doctors in a hospital | *A large group of soldiers trained to fight for a country | A group of tourists visiting Ukraine
test: Ella says «an army of volunteers» means just two helpers. What is the right meaning? | Two helpers who are very tired | *A very large group of volunteers working together | A group of soldiers marching to the park | A single helper who is very busy
exam: Nadia says «an army of helpers» means only two people, so the word must be wrong. What is the best answer? | Yes, two helpers is exactly what an army is | No, an army can only be made of soldiers, so the word cannot be used for helpers at all | *No, an army is a very large group of people doing something together, so two would be too few | Yes, but only when the helpers are wearing uniforms
